        "text": "Create four unassisted festival-themed items, each giving a total number of festival items (for example 12, 18, 24, 36) and asking the learner to list ALL factor pairs, in order, and state how they knew to stop. Do not accept partial lists as correct. Record which pairs were listed and which were omitted for each item, and score completeness separately from correctness of the pairs given. Decision: Confirmed unassisted graded returned work (returned-work:669be60869481a232004) supported three of four preregistered predictions at accuracy 1.0 within the 0.7-1.0 band: equal_groups (evaluation:86e6e05171057405, observation:d10841711c10da43, observation:c72a40b8f1c7c115), missing_factor (evaluation:40d7ae3df4699f1f, observation:49041448769f85c1), and word_problem_interpretation (evaluation:b2a57734e58c17cf, observation:1aefc03189d41337, observation:2502a56cc2b976a6, observation:59d86ebcaa44dfd2), with the predicted prior missing-factor and interpretation errors not recurring. The factor_pairs prediction missed its band (evaluation:69fa6e2c9629cc52, observation:18eacd211fb13b53; observed 0 vs min 0.7, prediction error 0.7), and the single observed error matched the preregistered pattern of an incomplete response when multiple factor pairs are requested. This is a scoped error on one construct rather than repeated contradiction across constructs, so the theory is revised rather than falsified. The single factor_pairs item is also too thin to distinguish a stable gap from a one-item slip, so mastery is not asserted from the three supported predictions alone. Evidence references: observation:d10841711c10da43, observation:1aefc03189d41337, observation:49041448769f85c1, observation:2502a56cc2b976a6, observation:59d86ebcaa44dfd2, observation:c72a40b8f1c7c115, observation:18eacd211fb13b53, observation:ce21f1bfd789aa65. Do not reuse exposed item identities or exact prompts: LAB-MATH-C:item:1, LAB-MATH-C:item:2, LAB-MATH-C:item:3, LAB-MATH-C:item:4, LAB-MATH-C:item:5, LAB-MATH-C:item:6, LAB-MATH-C:item:7, LAB-MATH-C:item:8."
      },
